<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>



<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Ahu

//ahu// — Hawaiian: heap, pile, mound, cairn; altar, shrine; a sacred stone structure.
Used in spiritual and ceremonial contexts — the //ahu// becomes sacred through human intention
and accumulated offering placed upon it. A landmark made from accumulation; addressable because
it has been named and tended.

A child-slot sigil. Each `ahu` block declares a named scope boundary within a meme — an
addressable child tiddler at `parentUri + slot`. The slot name becomes the tiddler title suffix.
Slots compose the structural skeleton of a meme's content; each MAY hold its own TOML meta header (set of tiddler fields)
and wikitext body.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ sense the slot name — a `#/name` anchor, rooted at the carrier; the boundary scope of this content unit
⏿ orient: child-slot, parent-relative addressing; slot name becomes tiddler title suffix
◇ parent at `lar:///uri`; this slot creates child at `lar:///uri#/name`; content stays inside boundary
▶ emit child-slot block node; deserializer produces a separate tiddler for each slot
↺ parent tiddler references child via `<<~ kahea ahu #/name>>`; child is independently addressable; confirm round-trip: parent body contains kahea~ahu summons; child has meta fields + content

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Law (Kānāwai)

An ahu block slot name MUST begin with `#/`. The slash roots the path at the carrier, so a slot names the same string it addresses; a nested slot extends it (`#/parent/child`). A bare `#name` belongs to no ahu slot grammar: a processor MUST preserve that source verbatim, surface a diagnostic to the operator, and MUST NOT normalize it or mint a child address from it. A CONTROL slot carries structural metadata rather than addressable content and takes no root — it opens no child to address.
A slot token admits `[a-z0-9āēīōūʻ-]` — lowercase ASCII letters and digits, a hyphen, the Hawaiian long vowels ā ē ī ō ū (precomposed), and the ʻokina (U+02BB); `/` nests, and `$` is reserved as a leading carriage marker (RULED, operator, slot-grammar-orthography). `lares meme normalize` folds a slot name — and only a slot name, fence-masked — to NFC first (so a decomposed vowel, a base letter plus the combining macron U+0304, precomposes to its canonical letter), then folds the three ʻokina look-alikes (the curly quotes U+2018/U+2019 and the typable straight apostrophe U+0027) to U+02BB, reporting each fold as a diagnostic. Kahakō and ʻokina stand RULED; a kahakō look-alike (a folding macron on any other vowel, or any other Hawaiian orthographic mark) is NOT ruled — it stays unfolded, and MUST pass through unchanged.
An ahu block MUST close with `<<~/ahu>>`.
An ahu block MAY nest inside another ahu block. A nested slot extends its enclosing slot path (`#/parent/child`), while a top-level slot begins a path at the carrier root.
An ahu slot MUST produce an independently addressable tiddler at `parentUri + slot`.
The tiddler representing an enclosing scope MUST reference each child slot via `<<~ kahea ahu #/slot>>` in its body.
Child slot tiddlers MUST NOT duplicate the parent's meta TOML — they carry their own.

The slot name `#/head` is conventional for the meme's primary content body.
The slot name `#source-shelf` is conventional for pranala edge declarations.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/syntax>>

!! Syntax

Decomposed at the wiki's causal island boundaries:

```text
<<~ ahu #/slot-name>>
content body

<<~/ahu>>
```

Compound kahea-ahu summons form (in parent tiddler body after decomposition):
```text
<<~ kahea ahu #/slot-name>>
```

Regex (open, canonical):
```
/<<~[^>]*\bahu\s+(#\/[\w-]+(?:\/[\w-]+)*)\s*>>/
```

Close tag: `<<~/ahu>>`

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/schema>>

!! Schema (machine-readable)

```toml
sigil          = "ahu"
kind           = "child-slot"
layer          = "block"
default-family = null

open-pattern  = '<<~[^>]*\bahu\s+(#\/[\w-]+(?:\/[\w-]+)*)\s*>>'
close-pattern = '<<~\/ahu\s*>>'

[captures]
slot = 1
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/quoteblock-floor>>

!! The quoteblock floor — un-decomposable content fences, never drops

Content that will not decompose fences to a quoteblock. The fence stands as the artifact a writer surfaces to the operator: a demotion, never an overwrite, never a drop.

The grain matches the write that produces the un-decomposable content:

* ''Whole-chunk ingest'' — a carrier arrives through the deserializer, or from outside the wiki into it, whole and partially un-decomposable. The whole chunk quoteblocks; no family stands yet at that point, so the carrier is the only grain available.
* ''In-place ahu update'' — an ahu tiddler that already stands, edited to un-decomposable content. ONLY that ahu's body quoteblocks; the `<<~ ahu #/slot>>…<<~/ahu>>` wrapper survives untouched, and the rest of the family stands untouched. A paste into the live TW5 browser counts as a write: the save lands in the CRDT store, and the house projects it back to disk — so this grain governs there too (fix on write).

A fenced span needs no new law to keep the ahu-fidelity guard honest. Fence-mask covers it (#/syntax, #/schema; the shared scanner at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-ast/ahu-scan.ts`), so the span declares zero slots, so `collectAhuSlots` finds nothing to drop. Un-decomposable content can never mint a phantom slot or a false conflict — the guard passes by construction.

Quoteblocking runs as a one-way demotion: every sigil inside goes inert until the operator resolves it. The surfacing rail that carries that demotion to the operator is NOT optional — a quoteblock nobody sees reads as a drop wearing a cure's face. Blast radius equals the write's grain: a per-tiddler edit never demotes the whole meme.

The ingest gate's composed-root dry run surfaces composition faults — a second live ETX, `frame-malformed`, `postamble-content`, an unbalanced ahu opener/closer — on the SAME alert rail the quoteblock uses. Refusal never happens on the stock syncer path.

This law lifts [[graceful-parsing|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/graceful-parsing#/recovery-policy]]'s panic-to-water floor from Layer 1 (the meme-ast builder, one sigil) to Layer 2 (the family split, one ahu or one whole carrier): water never regresses, never lies about structure, and composes with repair added later.

<<~/ahu>>

